---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import LinkButton from '../components/LinkButton.astro';
import { github, release, source } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Get started · Ostrilo"
  description="Install Ostrilo from the Chrome Web Store, set up your Nostr identity, and connect your first website. Source-build instructions are available too."
>
  <PageIntro label="Get started" title="Bring your identity along.">
    <p>
      Add Ostrilo from the Chrome Web Store, set up your identity, and choose what your Nostr
      websites can sign.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <LinkButton href={release.chromeStoreUrl}>Add to Chrome</LinkButton>
    </div>
  </PageIntro>
  <div class="article-layout wrap">
    <nav class="page-index" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="section-label">Install & connect</p>
      <a href="#install">Install from the store</a>
      <a href="#first-use">Your first signing flow</a>
      <a href="#build">Build from source</a>
      <a href="#questions">Common questions</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="prose">
      <section id="install">
        <h2>Add Ostrilo to Chrome.</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            Open <a href={release.chromeStoreUrl}>Ostrilo in the Chrome Web Store</a> and choose{' '}
            <strong>Add to Chrome</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>Confirm the installation when Chrome asks.</li>
          <li>Open Chrome’s Extensions menu, pin Ostrilo, and select its icon to get started.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Your identity stays in a local browser vault. You don’t need an Ostrilo account.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="first-use">
        <h2>Make your first signing decision.</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>Set up an identity.</strong> Create a new key or import your existing Nostr
            identity, then set your vault password.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Keep your backup.</strong> When creating your first identity, save the encrypted
            onboarding backup and keep its passphrase separately. Preserve an independent copy of
            any key you import.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Connect a Nostr website.</strong> Choose its browser-extension sign-in option on
            an HTTPS page. Decide whether it may read your public key.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Review and sign.</strong> Check the website, identity, event kind, and content
            in Ostrilo. Approve or deny the request, then see your decision in Activity.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          <a href={source('docs/key-backup.md')}>Backup guide</a> ·{' '}
          <a href={source('docs/managing-multiple-keys.md')}>Managing identities</a>
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="build">
        <h2>Build your own copy.</h2>
        <p>
          Prefer to build from source? You’ll need Git, Node.js 22, pnpm 11.5.2, and a desktop
          browser. These commands build the extension, rather than this website.
        </p>
        <pre tabindex="0"><code>git clone https://github.com/macro88/ostrilo.git
cd ostrilo
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm run build</code></pre>
        <div class="compatibility">
          <div>
            <span class="status-chip">Chrome & Chromium</span>
            <h3>Load unpacked</h3>
            <p>
              Open <code>chrome://extensions</code>, enable Developer mode, and choose{' '}
              <strong>Load unpacked</strong>. Select <code>.output/chrome-mv3</code> from your
              extension checkout, then pin Ostrilo.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="status-chip">Firefox development build</span>
            <h3>Load a temporary add-on</h3>
            <p>
              Run <code>pnpm run build:firefox</code>. Open <code>about:debugging</code>, select
              This Firefox, and load <code>.output/firefox-mv3/manifest.json</code>. Temporary
              add-ons are removed when Firefox restarts.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>
          <a href={source('README.md#build-from-source')}>Full source-build instructions</a>
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="questions" class="faq">
        <h2>A few useful answers.</h2>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need an Ostrilo account?</summary>
          <p>
            No. Your vault lives in the browser. There’s no Ostrilo account or developer server
            involved in signing.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use a key I already have?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. You can import an existing Nostr private key and keep the same identity. Keep your
            original recovery copy somewhere safe.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does the site get my private key?</summary>
          <p>
            No. It receives your public key after consent, or a signed event after approval or a
            matching permission rule.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I choose my own relays?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Manage relay addresses in Ostrilo’s settings. They’re used to look up and publish
            your Nostr profile.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where do I send feedback?</summary>
          <p>
            Use <a href={`${github}/issues`}>GitHub Issues</a> for bugs and suggestions. Include the
            browser, extension revision, and steps to reproduce. Use the{' '}
            <a href={source('SECURITY.md')}>private security process</a> for vulnerabilities.
          </p>
        </details>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
